      "type": "info",
      "text": "In a weekly report, you often **combine** functions to calculate and format answers in a single cell: nest one inside another, like `=ROUND(AVERAGEIF(range, criteria, average_range), 1)` or `=IF(SUMIF(range, criteria, sum_range) >= target, \"Goal met\", \"Below goal\")`. The inner function runs first and passes its result to the outer function."
